> Conclusion

Widening raises representational and arithmetic budgets, while dropout regularizes only the
residual branch. Exact mask and signed-shortcut checks explain that distinction; the visible
three-fit loop makes the comparison and its small-data limitations reproducible.

> References

- [Zagoruyko and Komodakis (2016), Wide Residual Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.07146).
- [Authors' implementation](https://github.com/szagoruyko/wide-residual-networks/blob/master/models/wide-resnet.lua).
- [CIFAR-10 dataset](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
